 "conventions": {
  "equirect": "three.js equirect mapping: u = atan2(z, x) / 2pi + 0.5, v = asin(y) / pi + 0.5 (v = 1 at the top of the image). azimuthDeg = u * 360 measured from the image's left edge. direction is the world-space unit vector toward the light with scene.backgroundRotation / environmentRotation = 0.",
  "hdr": "Ultra HDR (gain-map) JPEGs. Load with sky/decode.js (exact gain-map maths on top of three's UltraHDRLoader); the stock UltraHDRLoader also loads them but reads 10-30% low. Use hdrNoSun for scene.environment when a DirectionalLight provides the sun, hdr when it does not.",
  "sunIntensity": "sun.intensity is the sun disk's irradiance in the HDRI's own units divided by the luminance of sun.color: a DirectionalLight with that color and intensity, together with the hdrNoSun environment at environmentIntensity 1, reproduces the full HDRI's lighting.",
  "background": "background JPGs are display-referred (already tone mapped). Set colorSpace = SRGBColorSpace; three does not tone-map an sRGB background texture, so it matches a renderer using the same ACESFilmic exposure.",
  "textures": "ground textures tile seamlessly; RepeatWrapping with repeat = metres / tileMetres. ORM packs AO (R) and roughness (G): use the same texture for aoMap and roughnessMap. Normal maps are OpenGL convention (three's default).",
  "props": "glTF 2.0 JSON with the buffer embedded as a data URI, saved as .json. Textures are .webp next to it under props/tex/ (EXT_texture_webp, shared between props). Meshes use KHR_mesh_quantization. Load with new GLTFLoader().parse(jsonText, 'props/')."
 },
